WEBVTT


00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.156
Found it. 2777/8.


00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:14.512
Piernik, Shlomo.


00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.030
Piernik, Shlomo.


00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.994
What about Malinowski?


00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.837
Malinowski.


00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.551
Here it is. 3005/11.


00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.717
Goldberg, Izaak.


00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.834
There.


00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.675
And Stanis艂aw Nowak?


00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.038
Nowak. 2601/6.


00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.509
Simon, Hirshbaim.


00:00:53.160 --> 00:01:00.351
Simeon. Son of Benjamin Zelig,
blessed remembrance Hirshbaim.


00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:07.557
They took land belonging to
murdered Jews. All of them.


00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.639
Well, what did you expect?


00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:11.837
The Germans couldn't
take that land with them,


00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.917
and there were
no heirs left to claim it.


00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:42.640
Burek!


00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:49.590
<i>Go away, Yids!</i>


00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:51.160
Burek,


00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.754
you no good mutt...


00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:58.509
Come here!


00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.439
Need some help?


00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:51.875
I'll manage. You take Burek
and bury him in the garden.


00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.840
They shoot him?


00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.789
This ain't America.
Cut his head off with the scythe.


00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.200
I'll hold it in place,
you screw them on.


00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.514
I was at the registry
and stopped by the archives.


00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:29.311
A little more to the right...


00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:30.871
What for?


00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.952
There was something
wrong with the papers.


00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.680
Little higher, otherwise
the screw won't hold...


00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:37.911
This is our land, our father's,
our grandfather's, our...


00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:42.791
Our father's, yes. But Grandpa's farm
was originally down by the river-bend.


00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.514
It's all marshland down there. No wonder
he took this land during the reform.


00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:50.117
And where do you think they got
the land they gave Father from?


00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.192
It was the landlord's.
You know, Ko艣cieliski's,


00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.750
the one who fled to America, like you.


00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:57.594
The Ko艣cieliski estate only went up
to that side of the woods.


00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.355
The woods were theirs,
but this here land wasn't.


00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.436
Talk straight, will you.


00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.600
All these were Jewish farms.
From the woods down to the river.


00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:13.357
After the Germans killed the Jews
our people took their homes and land.


00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:16.319
All the reform did was round it off
so everyone would have 5 hectares.


00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.836
- How many of them were there?
- Yids? - Jews.


00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:22.274
Twenty six families.
Over a hundred people. Get it?


00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:25.114
Folks are scared of them coming
back and claiming what's theirs.


00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.715
In the old days they would've
set dogs on them, but now...


00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:28.870
the law's on their side,


00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:32.272
and there's documents
in the archives to prove it.


00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.677
Those Jews were all smallholders.


00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:38.560
The reform wouldn't have touched
their land. The law's on their side.


00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:41.076
If this was Chicago
we'd all be sued by now.


00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:43.436
- Are you sure?
- Swear to God.


00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:44.716
It's all Jewish property,


00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.351
all we can hope to get from the county
is that marshland Father moved out of.


00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:52.309
Lucky this isn't America and the Yids...
the Jews don't run things,


00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.199
otherwise it would
have been done long ago...


00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.592
- No one claimed it all this time.
- That's what I'm saying.


00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:00.639
Under communism nobody would have dared.


00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.440
Now they might not know
their families lived here.


00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:06.638
So now you know why folks
don't look kindly on you.


00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.749
OK.


00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:29.000
- We'll manage.
- Sure, why shouldn't we?


00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.510
Work's harder than
you're used to in America.


00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:47.357
Harder? Not harder,
it's no picnic in America either.


00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:49.910
Although here you're working
for yourself, and not some ass.


00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:50.877
Huh?


00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:54.192
I dunno.
Makes it all seem worthwhile...


00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:55.396
What?


00:05:55.560 --> 00:06:01.079
Nothing. J贸zek, let's go by
that river-bend later, huh?


00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.117
Maybe our old house is still there?


00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:17.393
- We're too close to the river.
- No we're not.


00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.199
Durign the flood,
the water reached up to there.


00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:22.114
The bed's normally
twenty meters narrower.


00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:28.034
J贸zek, anybody here still
remember the occupation?


00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:32.240
Nobody I think.
Some historian in 艁om偶a maybe?


00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.313
- Suds - how old is he?
- Eighty or thereabouts.


00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:37.352
Means he was a teenager during the war.


00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:38.670
Anybody older?


00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:40.877
They all passed away.


00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:42.918
Then there's old Palka,
must be a hundred by now,


00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:45.436
but you won't get any sense out of her.
Stone-deaf and senile.


00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:50.829
There's also Malinowski,
he's way past eighty,


00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.151
but they don't speak to no one.


00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:57.314
- Malinowski?
- The old man, his son and grandson.


00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:00.951
Edek's wife, the kid's
mother, lives with them,


00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.840
but I never saw them speaking
to one another either.


00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.957
- Strange, huh?
- You get all sorts.


00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:08.715
No one says you have to talk to people.


00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:13.794
What about the old madwoman?
That one who we were scared of?


00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:14.518
Come on.


00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:17.718
She was probably locked in a mental
hospital during Gomu艂ka's governing.


00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:19.360
She died there most likely.


00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:25.031
People in America keep saying that
Poles denounced Jews to the Germans -


00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:26.634
Jews in particular.


00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.634
No wonder, too.
Poles won't say things like that.


00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:34.520
Here it is.


00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:37.878
Jeeez... you think
that's our old cottage?


00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.997
Nothing else around.


00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:43.034
Pretty small...


00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:46.232
Way smaller...


00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:15.951
Let's go. Gotta get up
at 3:30 a.m. tomorrow.


00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:08.076
Fire! J贸zek, it's burning!


00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:21.510
Look!


00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.637
Over here!


00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:28.190
You fuckers.


00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.033
Come on, we'll go get them...


00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:32.751
We won't make it by ourselves.


00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:39.712
Tell the men to mow it down
along the road double quick,


00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:41.633
or else it'll all go up in smoke.


00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:44.915
Fellas, grab your scythes and
clear it as far in as you can.


00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.070
Dig!


00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:51.160
Why're you here and not
at our place? The fire's there.


00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:53.710
Get out of my face.
Talk to the captain.


00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:59.750
What are you doing here?
It's our field that's burning!


00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:01.593
It's too late to save yours.


00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:04.673
We're making a line to
stop the fire spreading.


00:11:04.840 --> 00:11:07.480
What do you mean too late?
There's a fire, you put it out.


00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:09.518
Let us have two engines.
Or one, at least.


00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:12.354
Don't tell me how to do my job.


00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:16.679
Send your men to my field
right now, motherfucker.


00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:18.877
Hands off, shithead.


00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:22.475
Kalina calm down,
or I'll have you arrested.


00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:29.033
Tell them to go to my field
before I fucking kill you.


00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:38.439
That's it, give them
Jews what they deserve.


00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:50.354
Out.


00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:58.831
I spoke to the police chief.


00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:02.671
In view of what happened to you last
night, the disaster that befell you...


00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:04.991
and of your condition...


00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:07.436
well, he's willing to forget
about the whole thing.


00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:09.398
He might be willing but I'm not.


00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:14.676
Now you see, Father, what bastards,
begging the Father's pardon, they are.


00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:17.674
- G贸ral, lock 'em up.
- Sooner or later, you son-of-a-bitch...


00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:19.718
- Shut up. - What?
- Shut up.


00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:23.078
- Says who?
- Says me. Your older brother.


00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:27.357
Thanks for bailing us out, Father.


00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:19.198
- It was arson.
- You can't prove that.


00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:22.478
In '44 they seized the farms
of all the Jews who got killed,


00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:24.438
and now they're afraid
they'll lose them.


00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:26.398
It's easy to cast blame on others.


00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:27.471
Not others.


00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:32.078
Our father took Wiemelman's
farm after they murdered him.


00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:35.475
When did all this happen?
I never heard the story before,


00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:38.678
and I read up on the history of
the parish before I took it over.


00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:41.116
There have to be some traces.


00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:45.877
The Germans executed 26 Jewish
families, over a hundred people in all.


00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:47.759
Much smaller Nazi war crimes
were investigated.


00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:50.958
They wouldn't have overlooked this.
And since witnesses are still around...


00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:54.079
- Malinowski and what's her name...
- Old Palka.


00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:56.630
Right, and Sudecki
has to remember something,


00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:58.951
even though he was still a kid.


00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:00.110
Mrs. Palka...


00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:03.478
Mrs. Palka is a patient
in our ward. God bless.


00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:06.949
- The Father asked me to fix you up.
- We'll be fine.


00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:09.553
If you've got a problem
with my grandfather,


00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:12.554
I suggest you take it up with him
and leave me out of it, alright?


00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:14.552
Unless you want to die of tetanus?


00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:22.353
- What's wrong with old Palka?
- Old age...


00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:34.631
Good morning Mrs. Palka,


00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:37.918
my name is Franek Kalina,
Stanis艂aw's son, remember me?


00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:39.070
Whose son?


00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:42.870
Stanis艂aw Kalina's,
lived by the woods.


00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:44.520
He's dead, that one.


00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:48.754
I'm his son, Stanis艂aw Kalina's son.


00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:50.115
Edek...


00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:53.114
Edek drowned, he was my older brother.


00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:58.393
I'm the middle one, Franek.


00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:03.313
I don't recall, it's been so
long, I don't recall.


00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:09.556
Mrs. Palka, remember
who stole your rabbits?


00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:12.315
Two bucks, your husband kept them.


00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:14.597
Rabbits?


00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:20.472
Sure, was the Kalina boy stole them,


00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:24.152
- but they never fessed up.
- I was the one who stole them.


00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:28.758
- I didn't want them to be killed.
- How's that?


00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:32.357
I'm Kalina's boy, the one
who stole your rabbits.


00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:35.672
- You're Franu艣?
- That's me.


00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:39.993
Mrs. Palka, do you remember the Jews?


00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:42.311
Sure I remember.


00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:44.756
Pretty boys they were:


00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:48.960
Abram, he was a pretty one,
such black eyes he had,


00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:55.037
all us girls were sweet on him.
But he only had eyes for that Helka.


00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:59.238
Way back when that was, they're
gone now, what's the use of talking?


00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:01.792
Mrs. Palka, what happened to them?


00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:05.478
- Abram?
- Abram and the others.


00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:08.157
The usual thing...


00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:11.074
Germans came and
then the Yids were gone.


00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:13.152
What year was it, do you remember?


00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:15.357
At the beginning of the war,
end of the war?


00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:17.193
Weren't no end of the war.


00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:21.593
Soon as the Germans came
they registered all the Yids


00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:25.595
- and the same week they were gone.
- Did they deport them or something?


00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:30.516
- To 艁om偶a? To Bia艂ystok?
- Who knows what they did.


00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:34.276
They was here one day and gone
the next, every single one.


00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:38.832
The Perlman boy hid
in the village awhiles,


00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:41.037
but wasn't a week 'fore
the Germans took him, too.


00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:44.477
- Whose place did he hide at?
- I don't know nothing 'bout that.


00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:46.040
Did he hide at your place?


00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:49.591
Heavens no,
mister, not on your life.


00:17:50.640 --> 00:17:54.475
People talk, you don't even
know how mean people are.


00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:56.472
They'll say anything
s'long as it suits them.


00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:59.360
Saying I sold moonshine and all,


00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:04.959
well, mebbe I did, and mebbe
I didn't, they can't prove it,


00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:09.273
but I never sold no Jews out.
Not like the others.


00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:12.193
Did you find out
anything from Mrs. Palka?


00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.033
I'm not sure,


00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:17.155
I'd need to talk to your grandfather.


00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.118
Grandpa was a teenager
when the war started,


00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:23.672
- he was just a child...
- Will you take me to him?


00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:26.355
- What do you need this for?
- What? - All this...


00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:28.955
As if I knew.
My brother got me into it,


00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:31.157
and then it sort of happened.
I don't know why...


00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:34.040
The more they don't
let you do something,


00:18:34.200 --> 00:18:38.956
the more they want to hide something,
the more you want to know.


00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:41.677
- It's the best reason I can give you.
- Contrariness.


00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:44.355
No. The truth. Only truth.


00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:50.316
And justice for all.
Stop here.


00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:12.916
What are you looking for?


00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:13.073
The tannery...


00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:16.755
They kept them here.
But not the Jews.


00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:42.480
Grandpa, mister Kalina
wanted to talk to you.


00:21:42.640 --> 00:21:44.916
Mister Sudecki, do you remember


00:21:45.080 --> 00:21:47.834
how the Germans took the Jews
from the village during the war?


00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:50.310
Sure I remember.


00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:53.394
Why d'you want to know, now?
Weren't your people, were they?


00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:55.870
But I got their farm now,
and I want to know since when.


00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:57.872
Don't be asking me.


00:21:58.200 --> 00:22:00.920
I mind my own business,


00:22:01.080 --> 00:22:04.312
don't care about other folks'.
So there...


00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:06.274
Mister Sudecki.


00:22:06.640 --> 00:22:08.711
Since when have you been
living in this house?


00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:10.553
A long time now.


00:22:10.720 --> 00:22:13.076
But you weren't born here, were you?


00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:18.390
I's born across the river,
like your daddy was.


00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:25.472
When did the Germans take
the Jews out of the village?


00:22:25.640 --> 00:22:26.312
What?


00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:31.836
- When did the Germans take the Jews?
- How do you know, they were taken?


00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:34.595
- Maybe you know then where?
- I don't, but I will.


00:22:34.760 --> 00:22:37.798
You won't know anything,
if it didn't happen at all.


00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:41.237
- What do you mean?
- Don't be asking me,


00:22:41.400 --> 00:22:43.676
better ask around your house...


00:22:44.480 --> 00:22:46.995
- Whaddya want with Gramps?
- Get your ass outta here, right now.


00:22:47.160 --> 00:22:49.311
- What's with the two of you?
- Get her in the house.


00:22:50.240 --> 00:22:54.359
- Let me go. Hands off, that hurts.
- Shut up or I'll smack you one. Ma!


00:22:54.520 --> 00:22:58.275
Don't appreciate no strangers
sneaking round this here farm.


00:22:58.440 --> 00:22:59.237
I'm just having a talk,


00:22:59.400 --> 00:23:01.517
your grandfather doesn't mind that.
Justyna invited me.


00:23:01.680 --> 00:23:05.720
Gramps is old an' all,
maybe he don't want to talk,


00:23:05.880 --> 00:23:08.759
an' I got a right to know
who's talking to him an' why.


00:23:08.920 --> 00:23:12.152
An' stay away from my sister
or you won't be seeing America again.


00:23:18.080 --> 00:23:20.675
- I spoke to Palka.
- And?


00:23:21.760 --> 00:23:25.800
She said the Germans took the Jews
in the Summer of 1941,


00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:28.680
but that still doesn't explain
why no one knows about it.


00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:31.309
Maybe they do, only we don't.


00:23:31.480 --> 00:23:33.790
The priest said he studied
the history of the region


00:23:33.960 --> 00:23:35.713
and didn't find any mention
of deportations.


00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:37.712
Go on.


00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:40.679
I spoke with old Suds,
Sudecki that is,


00:23:40.840 --> 00:23:43.196
- and he said something odd.
- Namely?


00:23:43.360 --> 00:23:45.397
That I should ask around our house.


00:23:45.560 --> 00:23:47.756
But he didn't say whom.
He can't have meant you?


00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:51.470
Maybe he didn't mean
anything particular?


00:23:52.040 --> 00:23:54.919
Maybe this was about
the house generally.


00:23:55.080 --> 00:23:58.551
So I told you, that I would have found
some documents during the renovation.


00:23:58.720 --> 00:24:00.234
Even the floor was changed in '80...


00:24:00.400 --> 00:24:02.517
He didn't mean documents,
but the house.


00:24:02.680 --> 00:24:05.070
You are really stubborn.
I renovated my house.


00:24:05.240 --> 00:24:09.029
But your house isn't ours
father's. It is by the river.


00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:12.197
There is nothing there,
you saw it.


00:24:13.040 --> 00:24:14.997
Let's go there once more.


00:24:15.160 --> 00:24:17.436
Maybe the house
will tell us something


00:24:17.600 --> 00:24:22.834
- what people are afraid of to think.
- Franek, come on.


00:24:23.520 --> 00:24:25.477
What can the house tell us?


00:24:26.240 --> 00:24:29.119
That the Germans never deported
the Jews from our village.


00:24:29.280 --> 00:24:30.634
Meaning what?


00:24:31.280 --> 00:24:33.397
Meaning that they're still here.


00:24:47.360 --> 00:24:50.114
- Where do we dig?
- Anywhere inside.


00:26:28.720 --> 00:26:31.997
Like my cigs, you son-of-a-bitch?


00:26:32.360 --> 00:26:34.397
Go ahead and choke on them.


00:26:34.560 --> 00:26:36.995
I had twenty packs in that bag.


00:26:37.440 --> 00:26:40.558
You could at least
chuck one over here...


00:27:01.840 --> 00:27:03.957
There's nothing here...


00:28:11.160 --> 00:28:14.039
Hail Mary full of grace,
The Lord is with thee.


00:28:14.200 --> 00:28:16.237
Blessed art thou among women


00:28:16.400 --> 00:28:19.393
and blessed is the
fruit of thy womb, Jesus.


00:28:20.320 --> 00:28:23.631
Holy Mary, Mother of God,
pray for us sinners,


00:28:23.800 --> 00:28:27.350
now and at the hour
of our death.


00:28:59.040 --> 00:29:02.158
- Grace be to you...
- And peace from God.


00:29:04.480 --> 00:29:08.952
Found them at last,
the poor souls.


00:29:10.600 --> 00:29:14.799
Why don't you bury them
in that graveyard you made.


00:29:14.960 --> 00:29:18.840
We'll bury them, mother.
You live in the woods?


00:29:19.000 --> 00:29:20.912
God granting.


00:29:22.040 --> 00:29:23.952
Did you see what happened here?


00:29:24.400 --> 00:29:26.232
Everybody saw it.


00:29:26.760 --> 00:29:30.356
They herded them into the Kalinas'
cottage then set fire to it.


00:29:30.520 --> 00:29:33.592
Laughing, drinking vodka.


00:29:35.600 --> 00:29:38.399
'That's for Jesus on the cross,'
they hollered,


00:29:38.560 --> 00:29:42.918
and inside the young 'uns were crying,


00:29:44.080 --> 00:29:46.231
all crying,


00:29:47.720 --> 00:29:53.990
and then there was only
the silence and the dying.


00:29:54.840 --> 00:29:59.915
The soldiers shouted it was
for Jesus? And drank vodka?


00:30:00.080 --> 00:30:02.072
Weren't no soldiers here.


00:30:02.240 --> 00:30:07.713
Mothers threw the wee'uns
outside to save them,


00:30:08.120 --> 00:30:11.830
and they pitched them
back into the fire...


00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:13.150
Lord have mercy.


00:30:14.320 --> 00:30:15.959
They were only children.


00:30:16.120 --> 00:30:18.157
You're saying there weren't
any soldiers, mother?


00:30:18.320 --> 00:30:20.357
They could have worn
black uniforms,


00:30:20.520 --> 00:30:22.751
not green but black with
skulls on the collars...


00:30:22.920 --> 00:30:26.516
Listen to me, mother. You didn't
see any Germans in green uniforms,


00:30:26.680 --> 00:30:28.239
but they might have worn black...


00:30:28.400 --> 00:30:33.794
Them with the skulls came by car
a day before then. Two of them.


00:30:33.960 --> 00:30:36.236
They spoke to the Head,


00:30:36.400 --> 00:30:40.440
Malinowski that is, and went
back where they came from...


00:30:40.600 --> 00:30:43.877
Weren't no Germans hereabouts.


00:30:44.400 --> 00:30:46.198
What do you mean
there were no Germans?


00:30:46.360 --> 00:30:49.159
So who got them in the cottage
and set them on fire?


00:30:49.320 --> 00:30:51.630
Everybody, the whole village.


00:30:52.120 --> 00:30:55.955
Everybody?
What do you mean everybody?


00:30:56.960 --> 00:31:00.397
Was Malinowski lit the fire himself,


00:31:00.560 --> 00:31:04.918
- along with one other fellow...
- You saw it all, mother?


00:31:05.080 --> 00:31:08.756
You Saw it? You were here
or you were told by the others?


00:31:08.920 --> 00:31:13.358
Stood right there,
crying to let them go,


00:31:14.200 --> 00:31:17.591
then the other one knocked me
on the head, made the blood run,


00:31:17.760 --> 00:31:23.916
and says, if you feel sorry for them
you old bitch, you can join them inside,


00:31:26.080 --> 00:31:28.754
and I was so scared.


00:31:28.920 --> 00:31:30.593
I wanted to live.


00:31:30.880 --> 00:31:35.352
As if them Jews didn't?


00:32:11.920 --> 00:32:13.513
What do you want?


00:32:14.240 --> 00:32:16.550
We dug up Jewish
bones in our old house.


00:32:16.720 --> 00:32:19.599
- What business is that of mine?
- Folks say you burned them to death.


00:32:19.760 --> 00:32:22.400
Folks say all sorts of things.
Damned if I care.


00:32:22.560 --> 00:32:24.119
Where's your son?


00:32:24.680 --> 00:32:28.469
Just me here.
As should you be - alone.


00:32:28.960 --> 00:32:30.280
Just you and me.


00:32:30.440 --> 00:32:33.160
Recognize my brother? From America.


00:32:35.200 --> 00:32:40.275
Your brother I don't mind,
but it's none of my kids' business.


00:32:40.440 --> 00:32:43.831
- So who burned them to death if not you?
- Ain't worth talking about.


00:32:44.000 --> 00:32:47.311
No one said anything for 60 years,
and now they deserve a proper burial.


00:32:47.800 --> 00:32:50.474
They might not be Christians,
but folks ain't cattle,


00:32:50.640 --> 00:32:55.078
- they all got a right to a grave.
- You won't bring them back.


00:32:55.240 --> 00:32:57.800
- The dead don't care where they rest.
- You're wrong.


00:32:57.960 --> 00:32:59.758
Sons care where their
fathers are buried.


00:33:00.200 --> 00:33:04.672
- Their sons are down there with them.
- So who burned them if it wasn't you?


00:33:04.840 --> 00:33:07.480
Who? The Krauts.


00:33:09.560 --> 00:33:12.314
Krauts did all sorts of things.


00:33:12.480 --> 00:33:14.039
There weren't any Germans around then.


00:33:14.200 --> 00:33:16.795
The previous day two
officers drove up in a car


00:33:16.960 --> 00:33:19.634
and gave you the go-ahead
to kill the Jews. SS officers.


00:33:19.800 --> 00:33:22.395
The next day you rounded them up
in our house and burned them.


00:33:22.560 --> 00:33:27.271
I rounded up a 120 people all by myself?


00:33:27.960 --> 00:33:30.429
Dream on, Kalinas, dream on...


00:33:30.600 --> 00:33:33.672
The whole village helped you,
but you laid the fire yourself.


00:33:33.840 --> 00:33:36.912
Dream on, Kalina, dream on...


00:33:37.080 --> 00:33:40.312
Malinowski, how old are you?
Ninety?


00:33:40.480 --> 00:33:42.949
- Your time might come tomorrow...
- Might today.


00:33:43.120 --> 00:33:46.272
Tell it like you were confessing.
Did you start that fire?


00:33:46.440 --> 00:33:47.840
You think I'm afraid of death?


00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:51.914
One fears no death who
saw death as a regular thing.


00:33:52.080 --> 00:33:54.834
Someone for whom killing a dog and
killing a neighbour is the same.


00:33:55.000 --> 00:33:59.153
I didn't kill neighbours.
Don't tell if you don't know.


00:33:59.320 --> 00:34:01.471
I didn't kill neighbours.


00:34:01.640 --> 00:34:02.790
Neighbours not.


00:34:02.960 --> 00:34:05.270
But the Yids. Tell the truth.


00:34:05.440 --> 00:34:10.435
Tough man you are, Kalina!
You want the truth.


00:34:11.040 --> 00:34:14.829
Do you know if you won't choke with it?


00:34:15.520 --> 00:34:18.752
If it's a confession you're
wanting, then I'll tell you.


00:34:18.920 --> 00:34:23.199
The fire was started on
two sides of the house.


00:34:23.600 --> 00:34:25.910
And it was...


00:34:26.080 --> 00:34:31.633
Your father Stanislaw
Kalina was on the other.


00:34:32.240 --> 00:34:34.197
There's your confession...


00:34:34.480 --> 00:34:37.837
Bury 'em back and let 'em lie there.


00:34:38.280 --> 00:34:39.839
You're lying!


00:34:41.080 --> 00:34:42.196
You're lying!


00:34:42.360 --> 00:34:44.113
- J贸zek!
- Truth hurts, don't it...


00:34:45.880 --> 00:34:47.439
No... J贸zek, don't!


00:34:48.000 --> 00:34:53.029
- Die, you son-of-a-bitch...
- Who was there, bastard, you or me?


00:35:00.200 --> 00:35:03.955
Your father hacked them Jews with a saw


00:35:04.120 --> 00:35:08.876
and kicked Halszka Mintz's
head all over the road,


00:35:09.040 --> 00:35:12.829
'cause she wouldn't put out
for him before the war.


00:35:13.000 --> 00:35:18.519
He chased her, and then he grabbed her
hair, and smashed her head on the ground,


00:35:18.960 --> 00:35:21.919
he grabbed her hair,
and smashed her head on the ground,


00:35:22.080 --> 00:35:23.434
he grabbed her hair...


00:35:23.600 --> 00:35:26.320
And she was crying: "mama, mama..."


00:35:26.480 --> 00:35:30.440
and he smashed her head on the ground,


00:35:31.800 --> 00:35:34.315
'till he sliced her neck clean open.


00:35:35.520 --> 00:35:38.638
Is that what you want to tell people?


00:35:40.680 --> 00:35:43.434
I'll swear to it as a witness.


00:35:43.640 --> 00:35:46.314
Is that what you want, motherfucker?


00:35:47.120 --> 00:35:49.840
So don't be raising
your hand against me.


00:35:57.360 --> 00:35:58.510
J贸zek!


00:37:37.880 --> 00:37:39.712
So, what do you want to do now?


00:37:40.120 --> 00:37:42.112
Nothing. What's there to do?


00:37:42.280 --> 00:37:45.000
We'll bury them in the cemetery.


00:37:48.560 --> 00:37:52.998
If we start moving the bones
it'll all come out.


00:37:53.160 --> 00:37:55.755
The authorities will find out,
the papers will find out,


00:37:55.920 --> 00:37:57.991
the whole country will
be talking about it.


00:37:58.160 --> 00:38:00.356
The whole world will
start talking about it.


00:38:00.520 --> 00:38:04.070
I know them Chicago Jews.
They won't let it go that easy.


00:38:04.240 --> 00:38:07.870
In 20 generations they'll remember about
our village, Malinowski, and our father.


00:38:08.360 --> 00:38:10.477
That's their right


00:38:10.640 --> 00:38:13.155
and our hope, too. Maybe the likes
of our father won't be seen again,


00:38:13.320 --> 00:38:14.310
God permitting.


00:38:16.160 --> 00:38:19.551
We'll bury them where we found them.
Now, tonight.


00:38:21.560 --> 00:38:23.472
- What?
- No one will know.


00:38:24.320 --> 00:38:26.232
- But we know.
- And we'll take it to our graves.


00:38:26.400 --> 00:38:27.151
- No.
- Yes.


00:38:27.320 --> 00:38:28.197
No, J贸zek.


00:38:28.360 --> 00:38:30.477
This world is a lousy shithole.


00:38:30.640 --> 00:38:32.916
And we won't make it one bit better,
but you know what?


00:38:33.080 --> 00:38:35.276
We won't make it worse.
And that's something.


00:38:37.440 --> 00:38:40.638
Our family's done way more
than its share of evil.


00:38:40.800 --> 00:38:42.757
You ran away from all this 20 years ago.


00:38:42.920 --> 00:38:45.674
Go back to America, and leave
the whole business to me.


00:38:46.240 --> 00:38:47.720
- I'm your brother.
- You're not.


00:38:47.880 --> 00:38:49.394
I renounced you when you left,


00:38:49.560 --> 00:38:53.554
Father cursed you and nobody even
spoke your name all these years.


00:38:53.720 --> 00:38:57.475
Mother cried her eyes out for you
in secret, scared to admit it.


00:38:59.080 --> 00:39:02.437
My brother died in '80.


00:39:02.720 --> 00:39:03.915
Get out of my house.


00:39:04.080 --> 00:39:05.116
I'm your brother.


00:39:06.400 --> 00:39:07.720
Brother!


00:40:31.000 --> 00:40:32.673
I knew...


00:42:05.800 --> 00:42:09.476
Lady, are you nuts?
What if I hadn't hit the brakes?


00:42:13.640 --> 00:42:14.835
J贸zek?

